Q. 5 Let $\mathbb{R}$ denote the set of all real numbers. Consider the polynomial function $f: \mathbb{R} \rightarrow \mathbb{R}$ defined by
$$f(x)=\frac{d^{10}}{d x^{10}}\left(\left(x^{2}-1\right)^{10}\right), \quad \text { for all } x \in \mathbb{R} .$$
Here $\frac{d^{10}}{d x^{10}}\left(\left(x^{2}-1\right)^{10}\right)$ is the $10^{\text {th }}$ order derivative of the function $\left(x^{2}-1\right)^{10}$.

Then which of the following statements is (are) TRUE ?

\begin{tabular}[t]{|l|l|}
\hline (A) & The coefficient of $x^{8}$ in the polynomial $f(x)$ is $(-10)\left(\frac{18!}{8!}\right)$ \\
\hline (B) & The value of $f(1)+f(-1)$ is equal to $10!2^{11}$ \\
\hline (C) & The degree of the polynomial $f(x)$ is 10 \\
\hline (D) & The constant term of the polynomial $f(x)$ is $-\left(\frac{10!}{5!}\right)$ \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
Q. 6 Let $a, b, c$ be positive integers in arithmetic progression such that the equation
$$a x^{2}+b x+c=0$$
has only integer solutions.
Then which of the following statements is (are) TRUE ?

\begin{tabular}[t]{|l|l|}
\hline (A) & $c-b$ is an integer multiple of $a$ \\
\hline (B) & Both the roots of the equation $a x^{2}+b x+c=0$ are odd integers \\
\hline (C) & If $c=15$, then $a b=8$ \\
\hline (D) & If $b=8$, then $x=3$ is a root of the equation $a x^{2}+b x+c=0$ \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
Q. 7 Let $L$ be the straight line joining the points $P(1,2,-1)$ and $Q(2,3,1)$. Let $S$ be the foot of the perpendicular drawn from the point $R(4,-1,5)$ to the line $L$. Another line passing through $R$ intersects $L$ at a point $T$ such that the point $S$ divides the line segment $P T$ internally in the ratio $|P S|:|S T|=1: 2$, where $|P S|$ and $|S T|$ are the lengths of the line segments $P S$ and $S T$, respectively.

Then which of the following statements is (are) TRUE ?

\begin{tabular}[t]{|l|l|}
\hline (A) & The orthocentre of the triangle $P R T$ is $\left(\frac{23}{5},-4, \frac{31}{5}\right)$ \\
\hline (B) & The orthocentre of the triangle $P R T$ is (4, 3, 5) \\
\hline (C) & The area of the triangle $P R T$ is $6 \sqrt{5}$ \\
\hline (D) & The area of the triangle $P R T$ is $18 \sqrt{5}$ \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
Q. 8 Let $y=f(x)$ be the real valued function defined on the interval $(0, \infty)$, satisfying $y(1)=0$ and the differential equation
$$x \frac{d y}{d x}=y-x^{3} .$$
Then which of the following statements is (are) TRUE ?

\begin{tabular}[t]{|l|l|}
\hline (A) & The function $f$ has a local minimum at $x=\frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}$ \\
\hline (B) & The function $f$ has a local maximum at $x=\frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}$ \\
\hline (C) & The function $f$ is increasing in the interval $(1,2)$ \\
\hline (D) &
\begin{tabular}[t]{l}
If $g(x)=4 x^{3}-5 x^{2}+\frac{3}{2} x$ for $x>0$, then the number of elements in the set
$$\{x \in(0, \infty): f(x)=g(x)\}$$ \\
is 2
\end{tabular} \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
Q. 9 Let $\mathbb{R}$ denote the set of all real numbers and let $i=\sqrt{-1}$. Consider the matrices
$$S=\left[\begin{array}{rr}
0 & -1 \\
1 & 0
\end{array}\right] \quad \text { and } \quad T=\left[\begin{array}{ll}
1 & 1 \\
0 & 1
\end{array}\right] .$$
Let $a, b, c, d$ be real numbers such that
$$S T=\left[\begin{array}{ll}
a & b \\
c & d
\end{array}\right] .$$
Let
$$H=\{x+i y: \quad x, y \in \mathbb{R} \text { and } y>0\} .$$
Then which of the following statements is (are) TRUE ?

\begin{tabular}[t]{|l|l|}
\hline (A) & $\frac{b+i a}{d+i c}=i$ \\
\hline (B) & If $\omega=\frac{-1+i \sqrt{3}}{2}$, then $\frac{a \omega+b}{c \omega+d}=\omega$ \\
\hline (C) & If $m$ is an integer greater than 2 such that $(S T)^{2}=(S T)^{m}$, then $m$ is an integer multiple of 8 \\
\hline (D) & If $z \in H$, then $\frac{a z+b}{c z+d} \in H$ \\
\hline
\end{tabular}

