questions.text:
Two identical plates P and Q, radiating as perfect black bodies, are kept in vacuum at constant absolute temperatures $\mathrm{T}_{P}$ and $\mathrm{T}_{Q}$, respectively, with $\mathrm{T}_{Q}<\mathrm{T}_{P}$, as shown in Fig. 1. The radiated power transferred per unit area from P to Q is $W_{0}$. Subsequently, two more plates, identical to P and Q, are introduced between P and Q, as shown in Fig. 2. Assume that heat transfer takes place only between adjacent plates. If the power transferred per unit area in the direction from P to Q (Fig. 2) in the steady state is $W_{S}$, then the ratio $\frac{W_{0}}{W_{S}}$ is $____$

