Q. 5 Let $I=\left(\begin{array}{ll}1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1\end{array}\right)$ and $P=\left(\begin{array}{ll}2 & 0 \\ 0 & 3\end{array}\right)$. Let $Q=\left(\begin{array}{ll} x & y \\ z & 4\end{array}\right)$ for some non-zero real numbers $x, y$, and $z$, for which there is a 2 × 2 matrix $R$ with all entries being non-zero real numbers, such that $Q R=R P$.

Then which of the following statements is (are) TRUE?

\begin{tabular}[t]{|l|l|}
\hline (A) & The determinant of $Q-2 I$ is zero \\
\hline (B) & The determinant of $Q-6 I$ is 12 \\
