An organic compound P with molecular formula $\mathrm{C}_{9} \mathrm{H}_{18} \mathrm{O}_{2}$ decolorizes bromine water and also shows positive iodoform test. P on ozonolysis followed by treatment with $\mathrm{H}_{2} \mathrm{O}_{2}$ gives Q and R. While compound Q shows positive iodoform test, compound R does not give positive iodoform test. Q and R on oxidation with pyridinium chlorochromate (PCC) followed by heating give S and T, respectively. Both S and T show positive iodoform test.

Complete copolymerization of 500 moles of $\mathbf{Q}$ and 500 moles of $\mathbf{R}$ gives one mole of a single acyclic copolymer $\mathbf{U}$.
