questions.text:
A quasi-static cycle of a monoatomic ideal gas contains an isothermal process (ab), followed by an isochoric process (bc) and an adiabatic process (ca) as shown in the figure. The volumes of the gas are $V_{1}$ and $V_{2}$ at $\boldsymbol{a}$ and $\boldsymbol{b}$, respectively. If the cycle has heat input $Q_{\text {in }}$ and output $Q_{\text {out }}$, then the efficiency of the cycle is defined as $\eta=\frac{Q_{\text {in }}-Q_{\text {out }}}{Q_{\text {in }}}$. The correct statement(s) is/are:
[Given: $\ln 2 \approx 0.7$ ]
