List-I shows four configurations made of straight and semi-circular narrow tubes containing air. A sound wave of wavelength $\lambda=0.29 \mathrm{~m}$ enters these structures at the point $S$ and a sound detector is placed at $D$. Between the points $S$ and $D$, the sound travels only through the tubes. List-II contains the possible smallest values of $l$ (refer to the figures) for which the detector $D$ records maximum amplitude. Ignore effects of sharp corners. [Given $\cos \left(15^{\circ}\right)=0.97$ ]
Choose the option that best describes the match between the entries in List-I to those in List-II.

